<title>USA: Brazil coffee areas to turn much cooler - WSC.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee areas to turn much cooler - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Temperatures in Brazil's coffee-growing areas will average below normal in the next three days, then below to well below normal on Friday and Saturday, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said.</p>
<p>WSC said it did not anticipate any damaging cold at this time.</p>
<p>It forecast scattered showers and thunderstorms on Tuesday and Wednesday, with temperatures below normal and lows in the mid 40s and 50s F.</p>
<p>The outlook was for scattered showers and thunderstorms on Thursday. There would be a few lingering showers and much cooler weather on Friday, while Saturday would be fair and cool.</p>
<p>East-central Brazil had showers and thunderstorms on Monday, with rainfall of 0.03-1.05 inches and 80-90 percent coverage. Highs were 84-90 F.</p>
</text>
